WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.394
This one is for the night you had a drink, fell asleep easily, and then woke at three like a light switch.

00:00:07.344 --> 00:00:14.123
If that is what happened, the night is not a mystery and it is not a relapse of your insomnia.

00:00:14.123 --> 00:00:17.844
It is a rebound, and it is almost mechanical.

00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:19.682
Here is the shape of it.

00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:25.564
Alcohol is a sedative on the way in, so you go down fast and you go down deep.

00:00:25.564 --> 00:00:32.785
Then your body clears it, and the sedation lifts in the second half of the night while the rebound rises in its place.

00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:43.094
Deep sleep gets front loaded, dream sleep gets pushed back and then comes in a rush, your heart rate sits higher than usual and your temperature is up.

00:00:43.094 --> 00:00:47.652
So you surface, fully, several hours before you meant to.

00:00:47.652 --> 00:00:49.608
Add the smaller things.

00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:54.549
You are dehydrated, your bladder is full, and blood sugar is low.

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:57.226
All of them push in the same direction.

00:00:57.226 --> 00:01:00.638
None of this means the protocol stopped working.

00:01:00.638 --> 00:01:05.741
It means last night had a chemical in it that the protocol does not control.

00:01:05.741 --> 00:01:14.211
Tonight the job is the same as always, and tomorrow the job is to not let one drinking night become three bad ones.

00:01:14.211 --> 00:01:15.741
So, right now.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:22.785
Drink some water if you are thirsty, use the bathroom if you need to, and keep the lights low doing both.

00:01:22.785 --> 00:01:25.270
That is the whole physical part.

00:01:35.452 --> 00:01:39.187
Back in bed, do not chase the sleep you think you are owed.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:48.960
You had four or five hours of heavy sleep and your body knows it, so sleep pressure is genuinely lower than it would be at three on a normal night.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.725
Lying there insisting is how a chemical wake turns into a conditioned one.

00:01:53.725 --> 00:02:00.254
Set your jaw loose, drop your shoulders, and let the out breath get longer than the in breath.

00:02:00.254 --> 00:02:01.666
No counting.

00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:03.651
Just longer out than in.

00:02:23.836 --> 00:02:28.733
If you are wired rather than heavy after twenty minutes or so, get up.

00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:35.521
Chair, low light, something boring to read, back to bed when your eyes close on their own.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.536
Same as any other night.

00:02:37.536 --> 00:02:41.197
The rules do not change because the cause changed.

00:03:26.356 --> 00:03:30.561
Tomorrow, four things, and they matter more than tonight does.

00:03:30.511 --> 00:03:32.247
Normal wake time.

00:03:32.247 --> 00:03:33.600
Not later.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:41.732
The temptation after a drinking night is to sleep in, and sleeping in is what carries the damage into the next night.

00:03:41.732 --> 00:03:45.100
Light and water in the first half hour.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.158
Both of them cost nothing.

00:03:47.158 --> 00:03:51.526
Caffeine as usual in the morning, and stop by midday.

00:03:51.526 --> 00:03:54.114
You will want a third and a fourth.

00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:56.467
That is the rebound talking.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.953
And do not go to bed early to make up for it.

00:03:59.953 --> 00:04:02.276
Same bedtime, or later.

00:04:02.276 --> 00:04:05.511
One last thing worth knowing, said plainly.

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:15.703
Alcohol within about three hours of bed is the version of this that costs you the most, and the cost lands in the second half of the night every time.

00:04:15.703 --> 00:04:18.379
That is not a rule about drinking.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:22.232
It is a rule about timing, and you can use it or not.

00:04:22.232 --> 00:04:24.408
Tonight is explained.

00:04:24.408 --> 00:04:28.217
Close your eyes and let it be a normal night from here.
